00:45:07.420 --> 00:45:25.660
Sophie Bulloch: I need to create a token, I need to create an account, I need to create a key, I need to do all of these things, and I need to connect to the Hedera network. This is really overwhelming for a new starter, even though, for me, at the time, this sounded like, okay, this is easy, we have lots of examples of other functions being good first.

384
00:45:25.840 --> 00:45:36.480
Sophie Bulloch: other examples being created. Of course, they can just look at an example and know how to do this, but we were hit quite hard with that when we realized that that's actually a really difficult task.

385
00:45:37.650 --> 00:45:41.439
Sophie Bulloch: So that's something that's… that's not successful. So anything that…

386
00:45:41.590 --> 00:45:47.859
Sophie Bulloch: pulls DLT-specific, or the… that pulls too much functionality from

387
00:45:48.030 --> 00:45:52.259
Sophie Bulloch: The… the repository can be overwhelming.

388
00:45:52.410 --> 00:46:00.890
Sophie Bulloch: We are still a young SDK, so our error handling is robust, but it's not necessarily detailed or that informative.

389
00:46:01.010 --> 00:46:04.999
Sophie Bulloch: So it's quite hard for a new starter to be able to debug

390
00:46:05.120 --> 00:46:09.890
Sophie Bulloch: Possibly the multitude of things that they face, which pull in lots of different files.

391
00:46:11.740 --> 00:46:17.259
Sophie Bulloch: Yeah, so even in the examples.

392
00:46:18.940 --> 00:46:28.420
Sophie Bulloch: have failed. Even, even, file renames have also failed, even though we have been very specific.

